Here's a simple 1-trace test to confirm that Pinchout detection 
and the Quadratic Programming routines work. Try:

% delivery ModelDescription.xml -PD -v 3 --Xsections 2 -RWS -N 500

% graph -TX -y 0 2 PosteriorXsection.fs0.mode1.t.*.txt

% deliveryAnalyser -i realisations.su -l | suximage blockinterp=1

% deliveryAnalyser -i realisations.su --histogram thickness 2 | graph -TX


and you can do this with samples from the prior by running 

% delivery ModelDescription.xml -PD -v 3 --Xsections 2 -RWS -N 500 -IS

for comparison
